ble to handle  both updates to many permits  and updates just to individual permits  ah i see so if you don't use  orchestration what do you use instead  then we use the other method  choreography where each service receives  messages  takes action on those messages and sends  new messages to the other services  so in what situations do you pick  orchestration and when do you pick  choreography instead  when the process is always the same  orchestration shines  for example when a car enters we always  save the raw camera data  the data is transformed from each  camera's manufacturer's proprietary  format to our standard data format  and then we extract the images from that  and save them into google cloud storage  finally we send the event data to cloud  pub sub for processing further down the  pipeline  that makes sense and when do you use  choreography when we have services which  may form part of a workflow but may also  be triggered individually  a good example is the permit group  scenario we talked about earlier  got it now it sounds like choreography  is based on having many triggers isn't  it messy to have lots of triggers all  over the system how do you manage that  complexity if you're using cloud  functions or cloud run services directly  in google cloud  it's really essential to maintain good  documentation and use a tool like  deployment manager or terraform to  deploy them  however if you're using the firebase  suite it's much easier to develop  test and deploy your cloud functions  there's even a great local emulator  okay does that mean that you prefer to  use cloud functions for firebase all the  time cloud functions for firebase only  support node.js and typescript which is  great for web developers but if your  team uses another language such as go or  python it may not be such a great fit  got it and which google products do you  recommend for orchestration and for  choreography respectively  for orchestration workflows is a great  product for designing orchestration  pipelines  workflows can be triggered by other  services such as cloud functions cloud  run or cloud scheduler  for choreography you can use event arc  to trigger individual cloud run or cloud  function services based on individual  events  however there are some services like  cloud firestore and cloud storage which  can trigger cloud functions directly  without event arc whenever an event  happens  okay and to recap when would you  recommend using orchestration versus a  choreography architecture  if you're developing a traditional  n-tier system on google cloud it's  probably best to use the orchestration  model  however if you're building a user  interface focused application with  something like the firebase suite  this is where choreography works really  well however  there may be times that you need to  create a hybrid app  in which case you can leverage the best  of both worlds  the best of both worlds i like that  thank you for joining me and sharing  your real world experience jason happy  to do it and thank you everyone for  watching if you have any questions for  jason or me add a comment below  also let me know if there are other  serverless topics you'd like to see in  future episodes bye for now  [Music]
 

